One of my favorites, though, is when Michael tries to set up Meredith.

1290
00:53:47.620 --> 00:53:47.900
Mm-hmm.

1291
00:53:47.900 --> 00:53:52.180
He says, so, Eric, you mentioned that you are in tool and dye repair.

1292
00:53:52.380 --> 00:53:53.300
I loved that.

1293
00:53:53.740 --> 00:53:53.880
Yeah.

1294
00:53:54.020 --> 00:53:55.760
Do you think he works at Crest Tool and Dye?

1295
00:53:56.160 --> 00:53:56.600
Probably.

1296
00:53:56.840 --> 00:53:58.500
It's on the sign down in the lobby.

1297
00:53:58.620 --> 00:53:58.980
Yes.

1298
00:53:59.180 --> 00:54:00.900
This is like a business park, right?

1299
00:54:00.920 --> 00:54:01.860
Yes, exactly.

1300
00:54:02.280 --> 00:54:03.540
Eric says, I am.

1301
00:54:03.880 --> 00:54:08.260
And then Michael says, well, Meredith recently had a total hysterectomy, so that's sort of

1302
00:54:08.260 --> 00:54:08.720
a repair.

1303
00:54:09.020 --> 00:54:09.700
All right.

1304
00:54:09.840 --> 00:54:11.100
I'll let you two talk.

1305
00:54:11.760 --> 00:54:14.760
Would you like a guest star breakdown on Eric?

1306
00:54:15.220 --> 00:54:16.060
I would.

1307
00:54:16.060 --> 00:54:22.540
He was played by Jason Rogel, and I found a very interesting crossover connection.

1308
00:54:22.880 --> 00:54:23.900
I know it.

1309
00:54:24.140 --> 00:54:25.060
Tell us, Angela.

1310
00:54:25.880 --> 00:54:29.460
Jason and I, when he played Eric, we didn't know each other.

1311
00:54:29.720 --> 00:54:34.420
But years later, we would both be in the Netflix movie Toll Girl together.

1312
00:54:34.800 --> 00:54:35.280
Yes.

1313
00:54:35.520 --> 00:54:35.860
Mm-hmm.

1314
00:54:36.040 --> 00:54:36.800
So crazy.

1315
00:54:37.000 --> 00:54:37.440
I know.

1316
00:54:37.580 --> 00:54:39.060
A little mini office reunion.

1317
00:54:39.260 --> 00:54:41.880
He played the doctor, the pediatrician.

1318
00:54:42.060 --> 00:54:45.800
When Steve's on, who plays my husband and I, we go to meet with the pediatrician because

1319
00:54:45.800 --> 00:54:48.320
our daughter is so incredibly tall at such a young age.

1320
00:54:48.420 --> 00:54:49.920
And he played the pediatrician.

1321
00:54:50.260 --> 00:54:51.680
Should we go to the restaurant?

1322
00:54:51.920 --> 00:54:56.060
We should, because Bob and Phyllis have not come back from the bathroom.

1323
00:54:56.540 --> 00:54:57.000
No.

1324
00:54:57.220 --> 00:54:58.780
And Jim and Pam are very hungry.

1325
00:54:59.040 --> 00:55:00.020
Their food is there.

1326
00:55:00.160 --> 00:55:01.500
This is getting so awkward.

1327
00:55:01.820 --> 00:55:04.940
They're discussing, when are you allowed to eat?

1328
00:55:05.800 --> 00:55:08.580
And Jim says, did you get hot food?

1329
00:55:08.720 --> 00:55:09.780
And Pam says, no.

1330
00:55:10.020 --> 00:55:10.900
She got cold food.

1331
00:55:11.040 --> 00:55:12.520
And he said, then I think you need to wait.

1332
00:55:12.860 --> 00:55:13.260
Right.

1333
00:55:13.340 --> 00:55:14.560
You have to wait for the other people.

1334
00:55:14.940 --> 00:55:17.180
And Pam says, Bob got hot food.

1335
00:55:17.500 --> 00:55:19.240
And I think his fries are getting cold.

1336
00:55:19.320 --> 00:55:21.280
And then they start eating his fries.

1337
00:55:21.880 --> 00:55:23.360
And then they eat his steak.

1338
00:55:23.580 --> 00:55:24.280
I know.

1339
00:55:24.620 --> 00:55:27.160
Did you see how I was really eating the steak?

1340
00:55:27.340 --> 00:55:28.160
Lady, I was starving.

1341
00:55:28.440 --> 00:55:31.240
I was, like, so excited to eat the fries and the steak.

1342
00:55:31.360 --> 00:55:31.920
That was real.

1343
00:55:31.920 --> 00:55:33.060
That's my real hunger.

1344
00:55:33.620 --> 00:55:37.980
I thought it rang pretty true, just knowing you the way I know you when you get hungry.

1345
00:55:38.280 --> 00:55:38.440
Yep.

1346
00:55:38.540 --> 00:55:41.420
That you would not hesitate to take food off someone else's plate.

1347
00:55:41.780 --> 00:55:43.980
Especially because they hadn't been on that plate yet.

1348
00:55:44.480 --> 00:55:49.240
When I was a caterer, would you take things and nibble?

1349
00:55:49.660 --> 00:55:57.940
You know, when I was clearing the tables, if there was, like, a roll or, like, part of a chicken breast that had clearly not been touched, I would eat it.

1350
00:55:58.000 --> 00:56:00.760
I mean, I was hungry and I, you know, was a struggling actor.

1351
00:56:00.760 --> 00:56:01.880
It was a free meal.

1352
00:56:02.020 --> 00:56:04.640
I would sort of piece it together from everybody's plate.

1353
00:56:05.260 --> 00:56:10.000
Let me tell you something, Angela, because you brought up food and eating for me.

1354
00:56:10.520 --> 00:56:11.840
You know it's important to me.

1355
00:56:12.960 --> 00:56:21.720
And it's so important to me, this idea of, like, being at a large dinner party and people are getting served food and when do you get to eat your food,

1356
00:56:21.840 --> 00:56:23.940
that I actually looked it up once.

1357
00:56:24.220 --> 00:56:25.420
Like the etiquette of it?

1358
00:56:53.980 --> 00:56:55.380
Yes.

1359
00:56:55.380 --> 00:56:56.480
Let's say a table of 10.

1360
00:56:56.960 --> 00:57:00.320
If I get my hot dish, I'm the fourth person to get it.

1361
00:57:00.440 --> 00:57:04.420
I start eating it because that's what the book said and because I want to.

1362
00:57:05.200 --> 00:57:06.760
But I digged a little deeper.

1363
00:57:07.000 --> 00:57:07.360
Okay.

1364
00:57:07.480 --> 00:57:10.060
Since we're on the topic of dining etiquette.

1365
00:57:10.200 --> 00:57:10.340
Okay.

1366
00:57:10.860 --> 00:57:13.540
Here are some other dining etiquette rules for you.

1367
00:57:14.700 --> 00:57:21.480
Apparently, if you get a dinner roll, etiquette says you should only butter one bite at a time.

1368
00:57:21.660 --> 00:57:23.480
You shouldn't butter your whole piece of bread.

1369
00:57:23.660 --> 00:57:24.360
Get out.

1370
00:57:24.560 --> 00:57:25.240
Isn't that crazy?

1371
00:57:25.460 --> 00:57:27.280
I'm going to put butter all over it.

1372
00:57:27.300 --> 00:57:28.720
I butter the whole thing.

1373
00:57:28.800 --> 00:57:30.020
I want more butter.

1374
00:57:30.440 --> 00:57:33.360
But if you butter it one bite at a time, you might get it.

1375
00:57:33.360 --> 00:57:34.020
You're double dipping.

1376
00:57:34.680 --> 00:57:37.680
But it, no, because you're using a special knife.

1377
00:57:38.220 --> 00:57:44.040
And you're putting it on your bread and you're taking a bite and then you're doing that knife on that shared communal butter again.

1378
00:57:44.900 --> 00:57:45.340
Etiquette.

1379
00:57:45.480 --> 00:57:46.240
I don't think you're right.

1380
00:57:46.440 --> 00:57:47.560
Well, that's what it said.

1381
00:57:47.700 --> 00:57:47.960
Okay.

1382
00:57:48.700 --> 00:57:57.080
Also, out of respect for the chef, you should always try several bites of your food before adding any salt or pepper.

1383
00:57:57.320 --> 00:57:58.980
Well, we always say that to our kids.

1384
00:57:59.400 --> 00:58:01.260
Like, try it before you salt it, guys.

1385
00:58:01.840 --> 00:58:07.280
If someone asks you to pass the salt, do you know you're supposed to pass the salt and pepper together?

1386
00:58:07.280 --> 00:58:07.940
I do.

1387
00:58:08.200 --> 00:58:08.980
They're a pair.

1388
00:58:09.180 --> 00:58:10.240
They like to travel together.

1389
00:58:10.500 --> 00:58:11.140
They travel together.

1390
00:58:11.700 --> 00:58:17.840
If you're enjoying a family-style meal, you're supposed to pass the dishes clockwise around the table.

1391
00:58:17.960 --> 00:58:18.580
Oh, gosh.

1392
00:58:18.640 --> 00:58:20.500
At our family, it's like a free-for-all.

1393
00:58:20.580 --> 00:58:20.840
Same.

1394
00:58:21.440 --> 00:58:23.600
Also, this one I found very interesting.

1395
00:58:24.360 --> 00:58:29.340
If you leave the table and you're in the middle of a meal, do you know where you're supposed to put your napkin?

1396
00:58:30.160 --> 00:58:31.660
To the left of your plate?

1397
00:58:32.020 --> 00:58:33.060
That's what I thought.

1398
00:58:33.160 --> 00:58:34.580
To the side of your plate.

1399
00:58:34.760 --> 00:58:34.920
Yeah.

1400
00:58:35.140 --> 00:58:36.000
Your chair.

1401
00:58:36.420 --> 00:58:36.760
What?

1402
00:58:36.760 --> 00:58:38.460
You're supposed to set it on your chair.

1403
00:58:38.880 --> 00:58:39.380
Gross.

1404
00:58:39.940 --> 00:58:41.640
My butt was just there.

1405
00:58:42.120 --> 00:58:43.600
Why do I want to put that up?

1406
00:58:43.700 --> 00:58:44.080
What?

1407
00:58:44.320 --> 00:58:44.880
No.

1408
00:58:45.320 --> 00:58:48.220
Maybe your hot feet were tucked up under your butt.

1409
00:58:48.600 --> 00:58:49.260
I know.

1410
00:58:49.260 --> 00:58:53.980
I could have a hot foot, inside-out, underwear, chair.

1411
00:58:54.300 --> 00:58:54.580
Yeah.

1412
00:58:54.760 --> 00:58:55.400
That's gross.

1413
00:58:55.400 --> 00:58:56.840
Why are we talking about my chair?

1414
00:58:58.340 --> 00:59:00.700
You brought up all of these things.

1415
00:59:01.560 --> 00:59:04.100
The hot feet, your underwear, and the chair.

1416
00:59:04.220 --> 00:59:05.380
This is all your stuff.

1417
00:59:06.300 --> 00:59:08.540
Why are you making me talk about this?

1418
00:59:10.580 --> 00:59:13.500
Pam and Jim can't take it anymore.

1419
00:59:13.720 --> 00:59:15.360
It's been so long.

1420
00:59:15.520 --> 00:59:17.540
They're like, did they ditch us?

1421
00:59:17.780 --> 00:59:18.120
Yeah.

1422
00:59:18.120 --> 00:59:19.240
Where are they?

1423
00:59:19.660 --> 00:59:20.960
Maybe they just left.

1424
00:59:21.480 --> 00:59:22.700
Well, they go to look for them.

1425
00:59:22.800 --> 00:59:23.100
Mm-hmm.

1426
00:59:23.500 --> 00:59:24.620
Over by the restrooMs.

1427
00:59:24.820 --> 00:59:24.980
Yeah.

1428
00:59:25.180 --> 00:59:27.480
And what do they hear moaning behind a door?

1429
00:59:27.860 --> 00:59:28.740
It is on.

1430
00:59:29.040 --> 00:59:30.840
They are clearly getting it on.

1431
00:59:31.180 --> 00:59:33.060
Jim and Pam are horrified.

1432
00:59:33.060 --> 00:59:43.090
When they come back to the table, can we talk about Phyllis chugging her water?

1433
00:59:43.250 --> 00:59:44.770
She's so flustered.

1434
00:59:45.230 --> 00:59:49.070
She's like sweaty, chugging her water.

1435
00:59:49.350 --> 00:59:52.230
Phyllis should get an Emmy for that moment.

1436
00:59:52.250 --> 00:59:53.690
She's so brilliant.

1437
00:59:53.990 --> 00:59:55.210
It's so good.

1438
00:59:55.370 --> 01:00:01.970
And then at 17 minutes, 35 seconds, can we please talk about the way that Bob Vance

1439
01:00:01.970 --> 01:00:04.850
holds his fork when he starts cutting his steak?

1440
01:00:05.390 --> 01:00:12.830
He's like got his fork in like a fist and he stabbed it into the steak and he's cutting

1441
01:00:12.830 --> 01:00:13.170
it.

1442
01:00:13.690 --> 01:00:15.230
He feeds it to Phyllis.

1443
01:00:15.350 --> 01:00:16.970
I had a question about this moment.

1444
01:00:17.090 --> 01:00:17.310
Okay.

1445
01:00:17.450 --> 01:00:17.590
Yes.

1446
01:00:17.770 --> 01:00:19.210
He says, do you want any steak?

1447
01:00:19.310 --> 01:00:19.970
And she's like, sure.

1448
01:00:20.110 --> 01:00:22.730
And he passes it over to her and she says, no mushrooMs.

1449
01:00:22.770 --> 01:00:23.930
He says, sorry, I forgot.

1450
01:00:24.390 --> 01:00:25.870
And then she eats the steak.

1451
01:00:26.050 --> 01:00:28.130
I was like, this is so nuanced.

1452
01:00:28.150 --> 01:00:30.170
This feels so personal and intimate.

1453
01:00:30.490 --> 01:00:31.410
Was this written?

1454
01:00:31.630 --> 01:00:34.710
And I went to the script and this is not in the script.

1455
01:00:34.850 --> 01:00:36.590
The whole steak thing, is it?

1456
01:00:36.750 --> 01:00:38.350
Him feeding her in the mushroom.

1457
01:00:39.210 --> 01:00:39.650
Wow.

1458
01:00:39.910 --> 01:00:43.010
That's crazy because I just remember shooting it several times.

1459
01:00:43.010 --> 01:00:46.590
So it must have been an on the day thing because it wasn't a one-time improv.

1460
01:00:46.910 --> 01:00:47.050
Right.

1461
01:00:47.050 --> 01:00:51.570
Because they had to set up that camera specifically to get that look from me and John.

1462
01:00:51.750 --> 01:00:52.030
Right.

1463
01:00:52.130 --> 01:00:55.670
And I remember that we had a hard time holding it because it was very funny.

1464
01:00:55.670 --> 01:00:59.110
But my question is, was the mushroom thing an accident?

1465
01:00:59.530 --> 01:01:00.490
I don't remember.

1466
01:01:00.510 --> 01:01:01.910
When he stabs the steak.

1467
01:01:02.070 --> 01:01:04.330
And maybe in real life, Phyllis doesn't like mushrooMs.

1468
01:01:04.330 --> 01:01:04.770
Maybe not.

1469
01:01:04.790 --> 01:01:05.670
So she just improv'd.

1470
01:01:05.790 --> 01:01:06.370
No mushrooMs.

1471
01:01:06.650 --> 01:01:07.330
I don't know.

1472
01:01:07.890 --> 01:01:09.190
It's so specific.

1473
01:01:09.470 --> 01:01:10.170
It's so good.

1474
01:01:10.170 --> 01:01:10.970
I loved it.

1475
01:01:11.330 --> 01:01:14.730
Back at the mixer, Michael keeps looking at the door.

1476
01:01:14.970 --> 01:01:17.410
He's really hoping Glove Girl will show up.

1477
01:01:17.550 --> 01:01:20.070
And Dwight is like, why do you keep looking at the front door?

1478
01:01:20.190 --> 01:01:21.030
Someone after you?

1479
01:01:21.760 --> 01:01:22.530
Okay, wait.

1480
01:01:22.710 --> 01:01:25.710
We got a fan question about that from Amy P.

1481
01:01:25.990 --> 01:01:30.910
She says, when Dwight asks Michael if someone's after him and Oscar says, why do you always

1482
01:01:30.910 --> 01:01:31.450
go to that?

1483
01:01:31.530 --> 01:01:34.230
Has anyone ever been after anyone in this office?

1484
01:01:34.490 --> 01:01:37.530
Amy says, um, yes, Oscar.

1485
01:01:37.810 --> 01:01:38.370
Roy!

1486
01:01:38.670 --> 01:01:39.130
Yes!

1487
01:01:39.250 --> 01:01:40.250
Remember Roy?

1488
01:01:40.570 --> 01:01:44.050
He was definitely after Jim and Dwight saved the day.

1489
01:01:44.330 --> 01:01:47.870
Listen, Dwight is ready with weaponry all the time.

1490
01:01:48.350 --> 01:01:55.910
There is a moment where a woman shows up who is not Michael's lady, and he turns her away.

1491
01:01:56.310 --> 01:01:57.230
Everyone groans.

1492
01:01:57.550 --> 01:02:01.710
I don't know that he turns her away, but she walks in and everyone is so excited for Glove

1493
01:02:01.710 --> 01:02:04.390
Girl that when Michael's like, nope, they're like, meh.

1494
01:02:04.750 --> 01:02:05.650
And she leaves.

1495
01:02:05.790 --> 01:02:05.950
Yeah.

1496
01:02:06.390 --> 01:02:07.670
This unnamed woman.

1497
01:02:07.950 --> 01:02:09.050
I looked her up.

1498
01:02:09.210 --> 01:02:10.350
Do you know who she is?

1499
01:02:10.510 --> 01:02:11.370
Oh, I do.

1500
01:02:12.590 --> 01:02:13.550
Dorian Frankel.

1501
01:02:13.730 --> 01:02:14.130
Uh-huh.

1502
01:02:14.130 --> 01:02:18.710
She was Allison Jones' casting associate for The Office after Phyllis left.

1503
01:02:18.950 --> 01:02:20.510
Let me tell you a little bit about Dorian.

1504
01:02:20.710 --> 01:02:22.510
I met her a lifetime ago.

1505
01:02:22.730 --> 01:02:24.110
Dorian, if you're hearing this.

1506
01:02:24.210 --> 01:02:24.510
Hi!

1507
01:02:24.670 --> 01:02:26.090
It was so fun to see your face.

1508
01:02:26.510 --> 01:02:31.430
We did improv together at ImprovOlympic, also known as Iowa WeSt.

1509
01:02:31.570 --> 01:02:36.930
We were on a long-form team called, ready for this, Fluffers.

1510
01:02:37.450 --> 01:02:37.970
Oh!

1511
01:02:38.230 --> 01:02:39.550
Dorian, do you remember this?

1512
01:02:39.550 --> 01:02:40.190
Most of you hear this.

1513
01:02:40.310 --> 01:02:41.450
We were on a team called Fluffers.

1514
01:02:41.590 --> 01:02:46.250
We would rehearse in her apartment, and she was lovely, and I'm so happy for her.

1515
01:02:46.370 --> 01:02:49.790
She recently won an Emmy for casting Veep.

1516
01:02:49.970 --> 01:02:50.390
Yes.

1517
01:02:50.910 --> 01:02:52.210
So she's amazing.

1518
01:02:52.490 --> 01:02:54.970
Dorian, oh my gosh, flash from the paSt.

1519
01:02:56.010 --> 01:02:59.670
So that was my other crossover connection with a guest star in this episode.

1520
01:03:00.530 --> 01:03:00.970
Amazing.

1521
01:03:01.870 --> 01:03:08.050
Dwight has kind of zeroed in on Rhi, woman who is dressed like Angela, but not for the

1522
01:03:08.050 --> 01:03:08.870
reasons we think.

1523
01:03:09.190 --> 01:03:14.630
Well, he finds out when they're talking that she works at a place that does catalogs for

1524
01:03:14.630 --> 01:03:16.630
community colleges and small businesses.

1525
01:03:16.930 --> 01:03:18.390
They must use a lot of paper.

1526
01:03:18.870 --> 01:03:21.450
I mean, at first we're like, is he attracted to her?

1527
01:03:21.590 --> 01:03:23.530
No, he's just trying to make a huge paper sale.

1528
01:03:23.970 --> 01:03:24.230
Yes.

1529
01:03:24.850 --> 01:03:28.950
Jenna, there was a lot in Deleted Scenes of like people just sort of chit-chatting,

1530
01:03:29.090 --> 01:03:32.190
trying to flirt, trying to meet people, make conversation.

1531
01:03:32.810 --> 01:03:35.050
Well, Creed talks to Lynn.

1532
01:03:35.630 --> 01:03:36.110
Oh!

1533
01:03:36.310 --> 01:03:38.530
He tries to strike up conversation with her.

1534
01:03:38.870 --> 01:03:39.670
You gotta hear it.

1535
01:03:41.700 --> 01:03:42.260
How old are you?

1536
01:03:42.680 --> 01:03:44.600
Wait, let me guess.

1537
01:03:45.880 --> 01:03:46.360
30.

1538
01:03:46.820 --> 01:03:47.540
No, no, no.

1539
01:03:47.860 --> 01:03:48.340
60.

1540
01:03:50.160 --> 01:03:50.640
34.

1541
01:03:51.220 --> 01:03:52.080
Cool beans.

1542
01:03:52.260 --> 01:03:52.640
Me too.

1543
01:03:54.000 --> 01:03:54.980
What year were you born?

1544
01:04:00.280 --> 01:04:00.560
Wow.

1545
01:04:00.840 --> 01:04:01.260
I know.

1546
01:04:02.020 --> 01:04:04.200
First of all, he leads off with like, how old are you?

1547
01:04:04.380 --> 01:04:05.060
Let me guess.

1548
01:04:06.160 --> 01:04:08.240
And then he goes from 30 to 60.

1549
01:04:08.640 --> 01:04:10.720
This is Creed trying to make small talk, guys.

1550
01:04:11.560 --> 01:04:17.940
I remember I was in a bar once and a guy tried to flirt with me by asking me how much I weighed.

1551
01:04:18.540 --> 01:04:20.980
And then he said, I bet I can guess.

1552
01:04:21.700 --> 01:04:27.260
And then he picked me up without my consent and then said a number.

1553
01:04:29.380 --> 01:04:31.740
Fellas, there's so much wrong with this.

1554
01:04:32.820 --> 01:04:34.980
I hope we don't have to break it down for you.

1555
01:04:35.120 --> 01:04:36.260
But like, don't do that.

1556
01:04:36.660 --> 01:04:37.040
Yeah.

1557
01:04:37.280 --> 01:04:37.920
All those things.

1558
01:04:38.180 --> 01:04:38.520
Yeah.

1559
01:04:38.820 --> 01:04:42.600
Don't say as your pickup line, let me guess your age or your weight.

1560
01:04:42.900 --> 01:04:43.080
Yeah.

1561
01:04:43.300 --> 01:04:46.660
Don't put your hands on a lady unless she invites you to.

1562
01:04:47.180 --> 01:04:48.080
So many things.

1563
01:04:48.180 --> 01:04:48.740
So many things.

1564
01:04:48.740 --> 01:04:52.960
But you know who did spark some interest in Lynn ultimately was Kevin.

1565
01:04:53.240 --> 01:04:53.840
I know.

1566
01:04:53.840 --> 01:05:00.740
And he's very charming in his just nervousness and honesty.

1567
01:05:00.740 --> 01:05:09.900
And doesn't Brian kill it in the scene where he shows that she gave him her business card?

1568
01:05:10.520 --> 01:05:19.080
It reminds me of that episode when they won their parking lot back from the five families.

1569
01:05:19.280 --> 01:05:22.360
And he's like, sometimes you just need things to go your way.

1570
01:05:22.480 --> 01:05:22.740
Yes.

1571
01:05:22.840 --> 01:05:26.440
I mean, I'm getting goosebumps just thinking about it when he does that.

1572
01:05:26.480 --> 01:05:27.360
Such a good actor.

1573
01:05:27.620 --> 01:05:27.880
I know.

1574
01:05:30.200 --> 01:05:36.580
Unfortunately, it looks like they're going to have to close down the party and Glove Girl never shows up.

1575
01:05:37.460 --> 01:05:38.700
Michael doesn't want to leave.

1576
01:05:38.820 --> 01:05:40.100
He wants to keep waiting it out.

1577
01:05:40.240 --> 01:05:41.740
And people stick around for a while.

1578
01:05:41.740 --> 01:05:42.820
It's very sweet.

1579
01:05:43.040 --> 01:05:44.200
Even Angela.

1580
01:05:44.680 --> 01:05:46.000
Even Stanley.

1581
01:05:46.680 --> 01:05:47.220
Yeah.

1582
01:05:47.720 --> 01:05:48.200
Yeah.

1583
01:05:48.540 --> 01:05:51.340
And Oscar's ultimately like, no, come on, Michael.

1584
01:05:51.440 --> 01:05:51.880
It's time.

1585
01:05:52.060 --> 01:05:53.300
Let's all walk out together.

1586
01:05:53.580 --> 01:05:54.540
We got mail.

1587
01:05:54.740 --> 01:05:55.060
Okay.

1588
01:05:55.800 --> 01:05:57.700
Aiden M wrote in to say,

1589
01:05:57.880 --> 01:06:05.240
Why did Michael never get to find the lady who left her glove in the blood drive van?

1590
01:06:05.420 --> 01:06:06.680
It has driven me crazy.

1591
01:06:06.700 --> 01:06:08.560
Even though he ends up with Holly.

1592
01:06:09.180 --> 01:06:11.380
And Diana P went on to say,

1593
01:06:11.640 --> 01:06:14.140
Why didn't this storyline continue?

1594
01:06:14.680 --> 01:06:18.880
I asked Katie about it because I was curious.

1595
01:06:18.880 --> 01:06:27.940
It just shows you how good of a job they did together in that scene that people wanted to see more of the blood drive girl and Michael.

1596
01:06:28.300 --> 01:06:33.140
Well, the message boards after this episode aired were all for Glove Girl.

1597
01:06:33.140 --> 01:06:35.400
And here's what Katie had to say.

1598
01:06:36.200 --> 01:06:38.540
Oh, man, you guys.

1599
01:06:38.900 --> 01:06:55.400
So here is the thing about my experience is that when I auditioned, it was with the caveat that it was a possible recurring character.

1600
01:06:57.160 --> 01:07:05.340
And so all I wanted was to perform well and to impress and to be asked back.

1601
01:07:05.720 --> 01:07:08.580
And it didn't happen.

1602
01:07:08.860 --> 01:07:09.980
It didn't happen.

1603
01:07:10.800 --> 01:07:13.880
And I'm sure they had their creative reasons.

1604
01:07:14.700 --> 01:07:19.080
But, oh, boy, I wanted nothing more.

1605
01:07:20.440 --> 01:07:22.280
But I'm happy with the time I got.

1606
01:07:23.080 --> 01:07:24.080
That's for sure.

1607
01:07:26.040 --> 01:07:30.120
So I will tell you, story-wise, why Glove Girl did not come back.

1608
01:07:30.120 --> 01:07:34.860
It was not because we were not completely charmed by Katie and her performance.

1609
01:07:35.040 --> 01:07:36.120
No, she crushed it.

1610
01:07:36.260 --> 01:07:37.120
Clearly, yes.

1611
01:07:37.800 --> 01:07:39.260
Michael has a talking head.

1612
01:07:39.260 --> 01:07:41.640
And it's really written in this talking head.

1613
01:07:41.640 --> 01:07:50.060
He says that this is the first time since Holly that he's even considered getting back into the dating marina.

1614
01:07:50.460 --> 01:07:51.100
Marina?

1615
01:07:51.380 --> 01:07:52.000
The marina.

1616
01:07:53.740 --> 01:07:55.440
Like Cupid's Sparrow.

1617
01:07:55.640 --> 01:07:55.820
Yeah.

1618
01:07:57.420 --> 01:08:05.940
And that was the story point of this episode, was not to introduce a new love interest for Michael.

1619
01:08:06.140 --> 01:08:07.260
They ultimately decided.

1620
01:08:07.700 --> 01:08:09.600
They were toying with this idea.

1621
01:08:09.600 --> 01:08:17.000
But really, it was just for Michael to feel like he could connect with someone again.

1622
01:08:17.280 --> 01:08:21.180
But ultimately, they're going to keep him on this trajectory toward Holly.

1623
01:08:21.400 --> 01:08:29.120
But because of this storyline, he's not going to be kind of as broken when he does finally reunite with her.

1624
01:08:29.220 --> 01:08:29.900
Does that make sense?

1625
01:08:30.260 --> 01:08:30.440
Yeah.

1626
01:08:30.680 --> 01:08:31.560
No, he's hopeful.

1627
01:08:31.920 --> 01:08:33.820
He's getting a little bit of his confidence back.

1628
01:08:33.920 --> 01:08:34.220
Yes.

1629
01:08:34.220 --> 01:08:35.340
And that's important.

1630
01:08:35.900 --> 01:08:36.240
Yeah.

1631
01:08:36.780 --> 01:08:38.720
Well, the whole gang is going to leave the building.

1632
01:08:39.080 --> 01:08:44.840
And Jenna, I just want you guys to know, when you watch us all exit, Mindy and I are just having a conversation.

1633
01:08:45.200 --> 01:08:45.860
Yeah, I saw that.

1634
01:08:46.000 --> 01:08:47.200
I'm gesturing to my hair.

1635
01:08:47.200 --> 01:08:48.660
I don't know what we're talking about.

1636
01:08:48.660 --> 01:08:48.960
I don't either.

1637
01:08:48.960 --> 01:08:49.780
You're very animated.

1638
01:08:49.920 --> 01:08:50.560
Very animated.

1639
01:08:50.620 --> 01:08:55.880
And then I feel like they sort of let us know that we were on camera because then I'd go back to Angela Martin.

1640
01:08:55.880 --> 01:08:57.980
And I do these little awkward waves goodbye.

1641
01:08:58.340 --> 01:09:01.080
But everyone is very pleasant and nice to one another.

1642
01:09:01.540 --> 01:09:01.820
Mm-hmm.

1643
01:09:02.500 --> 01:09:05.320
Michael's Lonely Hearts party was kind of a success.

1644
01:09:05.820 --> 01:09:06.160
Yeah.

1645
01:09:06.380 --> 01:09:08.800
I mean, they were all sort of lonely together.

1646
01:09:09.100 --> 01:09:09.380
Yeah.

1647
01:09:09.680 --> 01:09:12.140
This episode ends with a great tag.

1648
01:09:12.460 --> 01:09:13.400
It's so funny.

1649
01:09:13.600 --> 01:09:14.500
Found it very funny.

1650
01:09:15.020 --> 01:09:20.680
Stanley goes into the blood mobile, and he's got a little bandage on his arm.

1651
01:09:20.680 --> 01:09:22.980
He's got a cotton ball with a little bit of medical tape.

1652
01:09:22.980 --> 01:09:27.480
And he says, I'm so sorry, I gave blood earlier, and I'm still feeling a little woozy.

1653
01:09:27.680 --> 01:09:28.660
Do you have a cookie?

1654
01:09:29.320 --> 01:09:30.880
Can I have one of those cookies?

1655
01:09:31.200 --> 01:09:31.560
Right.

1656
01:09:32.800 --> 01:09:35.860
And she says, you know what?

1657
01:09:36.080 --> 01:09:39.480
You have a cotton ball and medical tape, but we're using Band-Aids.

1658
01:09:39.640 --> 01:09:40.460
Yeah, she's like, huh.

1659
01:09:41.040 --> 01:09:41.400
Weird.

1660
01:09:42.100 --> 01:09:44.460
And behind him, Phyllis walks up.

1661
01:09:44.840 --> 01:09:47.180
He's making a quick exit, and he just goes, Band-Aid.

1662
01:09:47.320 --> 01:09:48.540
And she's like, damn it.

1663
01:09:50.680 --> 01:09:55.660
And then Creed leaves the truck with his blood in a bag, or someone else's.

1664
01:09:55.720 --> 01:09:56.260
I'm not sure.

1665
01:09:56.600 --> 01:09:57.520
To go where?

1666
01:09:57.700 --> 01:09:58.520
To do what?

1667
01:09:58.680 --> 01:10:02.040
I don't know, but this is what Dwight has been worried about the whole episode.

1668
01:10:02.180 --> 01:10:02.620
I know.

1669
01:10:02.740 --> 01:10:03.620
Where is Dwight?

1670
01:10:04.480 --> 01:10:05.300
I don't know.

1671
01:10:05.860 --> 01:10:07.680
Well, that was blood drive, everybody.

1672
01:10:07.780 --> 01:10:09.380
That is blood drive, everyone.

1673
01:10:09.460 --> 01:10:10.520
I'm going to go home.

1674
01:10:10.620 --> 01:10:12.100
I'm going to put on different shoes.

1675
01:10:12.620 --> 01:10:13.480
Cool off your feet.

1676
01:10:13.580 --> 01:10:14.800
Don't put on any shoes.

1677
01:10:15.080 --> 01:10:16.500
Just take shoes off.

1678
01:10:16.500 --> 01:10:18.220
It's like 95 degrees out.

1679
01:10:18.440 --> 01:10:20.700
I encourage you to get a pair of flip-flops.

1680
01:10:20.960 --> 01:10:22.840
Yeah, and I guess I have to fix my hair.

1681
01:10:23.040 --> 01:10:27.960
Well, you do have one guy that's going, he's like at attention.

1682
01:10:28.960 --> 01:10:30.100
Just in your bangs.

1683
01:10:30.700 --> 01:10:32.240
I'm growing my bangs out.

1684
01:10:32.500 --> 01:10:34.140
Oh, it's a transition.

1685
01:10:34.400 --> 01:10:35.620
They're a strange length.

1686
01:10:36.400 --> 01:10:37.760
It was a summer thing.

1687
01:10:37.960 --> 01:10:39.160
We're moving into fall.

1688
01:10:39.960 --> 01:10:41.400
Yeah, you got to have your fall hairdo.

1689
01:10:41.560 --> 01:10:42.020
That's right.

1690
01:10:42.160 --> 01:10:46.140
I'm moving into, I don't know what my fall hairdo is yet, but we're transitioning.

1691
01:10:46.500 --> 01:10:47.720
Out of bangs right now.

1692
01:10:48.140 --> 01:10:50.440
I can't wait to see what your fall hairdo is.

1693
01:10:50.600 --> 01:10:52.240
Well, I know I'm going to get the truth from you.

1694
01:10:52.360 --> 01:10:52.920
That's for sure.

1695
01:10:53.060 --> 01:10:53.620
That's for sure.

1696
01:10:54.000 --> 01:10:54.440
All right.

1697
01:10:54.600 --> 01:10:55.780
I love you, lady.

1698
01:10:56.180 --> 01:10:56.720
All right, guys.

1699
01:10:56.860 --> 01:10:57.820
Have a great week.

1700
01:10:57.900 --> 01:10:58.920
We'll see you later.

